terraform init – Initialize Terraform in the working directory.

terraform validate – Check whether the code syntax is correct.

terraform plan – Show what Terraform will do before applying.

terraform apply – Apply the changes and create/update resources.
terraform apply - destroy  -  it shows the preview of destroy

terraform destroy – Destroy all resources defined in the config.
terraform destroy -target=resource  -  to delete the specific resource

terraform fmt – Format the .tf files properly.

terraform output – Show the output values after apply.

terraform show – Show full state and resource details.

terraform state list – List all resources tracked in state.

terraform state show <resource> – Show detailed info about a specific resource.
terraform state push - 
terraform state rm - 
terraform state mv - rename

terraform taint <resource> – Mark a resource to be recreated on next apply.

terraform untaint <resource> – Remove taint and keep the resource as-is.

terraform graph – Generate a dependency graph of resources.

terraform import <resource> <id> – Import an existing resource to Terraform.

terraform refresh – Update state file from real infrastructure (old method).

terraform workspace create